<title>UK: Crewman dies in tanker fire off Chittagong.</title>
<headline>Crewman dies in tanker fire off Chittagong.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>One crew member died in a fire aboard the Cypriot-flagged crude tanker Saraband off Chittagong, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence reported on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said that among other damage, the generator of the auxiliary aft engine set was completely burnt out on the 132,478 dwt vessel.</p>
<p>Temporary repairs were in progress and the crude on board was being discharged.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4088</p>
